 First, notice $2<\sqrt3<3$, and we apply Cauchy-Schwarz inequality
\begin{align}
& vicinity=[4+4\sqrt3+3]+[4-4\sqrt3+3]\\
&=20
\end{align}
<answer>So $(2+\sqrt3)^4=20+\overbrace{4+\sqrt3}=\delta>20$, and the nearest integer to this is $20$. $\square$</answer>

